1. d4 d5 2. e4 { The Blackmar-Diemer Gambit: White offers e4 to open the f-file. }
2... dxe4 3. Nc3 { Attacking e4 and developing. }
3... Nf6 4. f3 { Offering a second pawn to open lines. }
4... exf3 5. Nxf3 { A pawn down, but with a lead in development and the half-open f-file. }
5... Bg4 { [%name Teichmann Defense] }
( 5... e6 { [%name Euwe Defense] }
  6. Bg5 Be7 7. Bd3 { Aiming at h7 for a later attack. }
  7... Nbd7 8. O-O c5 9. Qe1 { The queen swings to h4 for a kingside attack. } )
( 5... g6 { [%name Bogoljubov Defense] }
  6. Bc4 Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. Qe1 { Heading for h4, then Bh6 to trade off the defender. }
  8... Nc6 9. Qh4 )
6. h3 { Asking the bishop: trade or retreat. }
6... Bxf3 7. Qxf3 c6 8. Be3 { Developing and preparing long castling. }
